## Feature-Specific Classes

Every new visual or functional vertical in the application MUST be isolated within `lib/feature_{name}` following this strict internal structure:

- `feature_{name}/views`: Contains the UI screen implementation (`{name}_page.dart`). **Every page (screen) should be implemented as a Stateless Widget unless it requires a StatefulWidget for specific lifecycle needs.**
- `feature_{name}/ui_components`: Local, non-reusable UI widgets tailored uniquely to this feature.
- `feature_{name}/models` *(optional)*: States or DTOs bound singularly to this feature's logic. They MUST follow the `*_model.dart` naming convention.
- `feature_{name}/blocs`: The `rx_bloc` files reacting to UI inputs to compute states (`{name}_bloc.dart` + generated files). **Complex BLoC implementation details can be offloaded to a separate `{name}_bloc_extensions.dart` file for improved readability.**
- `feature_{name}/services`: Middle-layer orchestrators parsing repository data for the BLoC (`{name}_service.dart`). Feature-specific services should be registered at `lib/feature_{name}/di` and will be accessible only within the feature.
- `feature_{name}/di`: Dependency injection initializing the BLoC and required dependencies (`{name}_page_with_dependencies.dart`).
